[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 15: 256-QAM.
# Eight bits per symbol on a 16 by 16 grid. Neighbouring points are only 2/15 of the peak amplitude apart, so even a little noise merges neighbouring points. Compare the matched-filter constellation here (SNR 35 dB) with 64-QAM in lesson 5 and check the PAPR and EVM in the Measurements block. Lower the SNR in steps of 5 dB to see where the grid dissolves.
Version=2
Modulation=256-QAM
NumberOfSymbols=2048
SymbolRateBaud=1000
SamplesPerSymbol=8
Pulse=RRC
RRCBeta=0.2
SpanSymbols=10
AmplitudeGain=1
DataSource=Random
